# SlayZone Environment Variables — Per Application

Reference of env vars read (**R**) or set (**S**) by each of the 4 SlayZone apps, plus the shared/domain code each pulls in at runtime. `(dev)` = dev-only, `(test)` = test/e2e-only, `(build)` = build-time (Vite `loadEnv`, not runtime `process.env`).

> **Standalone hard rule:** hub + runner must never use `~/.slayzone`. Enforced by seeding `SLAYZONE_ROOT=process.cwd()` at boot (unless supervised or an anchor is already set) → all state lives in CWD.

