### Child-process env passthrough
Runner spreads **entire `process.env`** into every PTY/proc/git-setup child, then applies hub-pushed `env` overrides (arbitrary keys — `PATH`, agent API keys, etc.). PTY sets child `TERM` via `name:'xterm-color'`.
- PTY: `handlers/pty.ts:48` · proc: `handlers/proc.ts:58` · git: `handlers/git.ts:161`

### Test-only
`RUNNER_TEST_VAR` (proc env-override fixture) `proc.test.ts:149`. *(`RUNNER_VERSION` is a code constant `'0.0.0'`, not an env var.)*

> **Scope note:** runner does NOT import `@slayzone/terminal` or the `@slayzone/platform` barrel at runtime — so `SLAYZONE_STORE_DIR`/`SLAYZONE_PORT`/`SLAYZONE_HOST` and the agent settings-path vars are **not** reached by the runner (they're hub/app-side). Only ROOT/HOME_DIR/HOME/USERPROFILE anchor it.

